From: Daniel Johansson <1911831+djohansson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix missing stdlib.h include

TracyStorage.cpp calls getenv() without including <stdlib.h>, relying on
it being pulled in transitively (e.g. via <windows.h> or MSVC STL's
<string>). Building against libc++ instead of MSVC STL no longer pulls
it in transitively, so getenv is undeclared:
  error: use of undeclared identifier 'getenv'; did you mean '_wgetenv'?
---
 profiler/src/profiler/TracyStorage.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/profiler/src/profiler/TracyStorage.cpp b/profiler/src/profiler/TracyStorage.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/profiler/src/profiler/TracyStorage.cpp
+++ b/profiler/src/profiler/TracyStorage.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #endif
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string>
 #include <string.h>

--
2.47.0.windows.1

